    description: "dispatch:F4 added function/variable to linkers/containment.py CONTAINABLE_KINDS, rooting top-level members at their file/class anchor. But 'field' was never added, so kind=field symbols (real class-body attributes, emitted with dotted names like 'Widget.name' via emission-parity F5/WI-jusus) get NO contains edge and are orphans. Self-analysis (/tmp/warm_vuzur.json): 1862 field orphans of 1870 total field symbols (99.6% orphan), 1846 Python + a few ts/rust/java/swift/go/csharp/js; these DOMINATE the orphan-ratchet ratio (6.18% overall). Fix (F4-analogous): add 'field' to CONTAINABLE_KINDS so the containment linker roots fields at their class via Phase-1 dotted-name parent extraction (verified on a fixture: 'Widget.name'/'Widget.size' -> Widget contains field, exactly like method 'Widget.area'). Per the containment module docstring the dead-code reachability BFS does NOT traverse contains, so this de-orphaning does not move the dead-code-maybe FP rate; it affects centrality (fields gain an inbound contains edge from their class) and reverse-slice class-expansion. Discovered while investigating WI-logon (file-anchor orphan-ratchet breach); field orphans are the larger, distinct root cause. Pairs with WI-logon (exempt kind=file) to restore the env-gated orphan ratchet."  # 36c2
